{
  "$comment": [
    "What the Python lint gates do not read, and what each omission shields.",
    "Consumed by scripts/check_lint_debt.py, which generates ruff.toml's three",
    "exclusion arrays from this file and re-measures the tree against it.",
    "",
    "MEMBERSHIP IS DERIVED, JUDGEMENT IS AUTHORED. `lintDebt` and `formatDebt` are",
    "produced by `python3 scripts/check_lint_debt.py --write`; do not hand-edit",
    "them. `scope` is hand-authored, because it is the one part that is a decision",
    "rather than a measurement.",
    "",
    "WHY IT EXISTS. ruff.toml excluded five bare directory names -- notebooks,",
    "options, patterns, src, scripts -- which match at ANY path depth, so 442 of",
    "1230 tracked .py files were read by neither the linter nor the formatter.",
    "Issue #975. Closing that surfaced 267 lint findings and 189 unformatted files",
    "at once, in trees that seven other branches were editing, so the exclusions",
    "were made per-file and ratcheted instead of being deleted in one commit.",
    "",
    "THE RATCHET. Naming a file keeps NEW files covered but leaves the named file",
    "unexamined forever, which is how an exemption rots. So every listed file also",
    "records the findings it shields, and the gate fails if it gains one, if it",
    "becomes clean (delist it), or if the path disappears. Same shape as",
    "METERING_KEY_EXEMPT in",
    "lib/idp_common_pkg/tests/unit/bedrock/test_long_context_metering_key.py:",
    "the exemption covers the sites audited when it was written, not the filename",
    "forever.",
    "",
    "FIELDS of a `scope` entry:",
    "  turnsOff    what stops being asserted for the paths it matches",
    "  premise     name of a predicate in scripts/check_lint_debt.py, evaluated",
    "              against this tree per entry",
    "  reason      the judgement itself, in prose",
    "  ratchet     what keeps the entry finite",
    "  ratchetGap  required when the ratchet does not pin the count: what is",
    "              consequently unprotected. An unmeasured gap is how this class",
    "              started, so the gaps are enumerated rather than implied away.",
    "  shields     re-measured by --write; informational, not asserted exactly"
  ],
  "generator": "python3 scripts/check_lint_debt.py --write",
  "scope": {
    "**/*.ipynb": {
      "turnsOff": "ruff lint AND format for every Jupyter notebook",
      "premise": "only_notebooks_and_they_have_their_own_gate",
      "reason": "E402 (imports not at the top), F811 (redefinition) and I001 (import order) describe a module; a notebook is a document run cell by cell, so they are not a quality signal there. `ruff format` would additionally rewrite every cell's source array, making notebook diffs unreadable. Notebooks are not unchecked as a result: notebooks/_validate_notebooks.py resolves their imports and symbol references against a real Python environment, which is the failure class that matters for them.",
      "ratchet": "non-vacuity + premise (the pattern must match only .ipynb, and the notebook harness must still exist)",
      "ratchetGap": "the count is not pinned, so a new notebook may add ruff findings without failing anything. Pinning it would red-line every notebook edit. basedpyright also excludes notebooks (pyrightconfig.json), where the gap is sharper: 10 errors, 6 of them reportUndefinedVariable.",
      "shields": {
        "files": 47,
        "lintFindings": 333,
        "unformatted": 47
      }
    },
    "feature-platform/pii-anonymizer/hook/vendor": {
      "turnsOff": "ruff lint AND format for the vendored copy of awslabs/pii-anonymizer",
      "premise": "vendored_with_provenance",
      "reason": "Third-party source (Apache-2.0), kept byte-for-byte so that .claude/skills/sync-pii-anonymizer.md can diff it against the upstream commit pinned in its PROVENANCE.md. Reformatting it to our style would make every re-sync a manual merge.",
      "ratchet": "non-vacuity + premise (PROVENANCE.md must still pin an upstream commit)",
      "ratchetGap": "the count is not pinned, because an upstream re-sync legitimately changes it. A defect introduced into the vendored tree by us rather than upstream would therefore not be caught here; the sync skill's diff-against-upstream step is what covers that.",
      "shields": {
        "files": 31,
        "lintFindings": 44,
        "unformatted": 3
      }
    }
  },
